  "id": "DrugBank_DB06176 - MONDO_15758",
  "verbalization": "Romidepsin is implicated in the pathogenesis of Primary Cutaneous T-cell Lymphoma (PCTCL) through a chain of indications that link it to the disease. The evidence suggests that Romidepsin may act as a potential therapeutic agent for PCTCL, as it is associated with Primary Cutaneous T-cell Non-Hodgkin Lymphoma (PCTNHL), a closely related condition. This relationship is supported by the presence of a direct indication between Romidepsin and PCTNHL, which in turn is linked to PCTCL via intermediate drugs such as Flumethasone, Denileukin Diftitox, and Mometasone Furoate. These drugs are known to modulate immune responses and inflammation, which are central to the pathophysiology of T-cell lymphomas. The cumulative evidence suggests that Romidepsin may exert a therapeutic effect through mechanisms involving immune modulation or anti-inflammatory pathways, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated. The integration of these indications supports the hypothesis that Romidepsin could be a candidate for repurposing in the treatment of PCTCL, provided further mechanistic validation is conducted.",
